<SddInterface keywords="interface, schema, versioning, compatibility, consumer, decision-log, sdd-interface" type="directive" ver="2.1">
  <Mission>
    Author or evolve an `interface` scope spec — cross-scope interfaces: schema (OpenAPI / gRPC proto
    / JSON Schema / GraphQL), versioning policy, compatibility matrix, consumer declaration. A
    self-contained living spec. Loaded lazily by the router; inherits the router core (language,
    dialogue, safeguard, diverge, no-narration, stateless) — not repeated here.

    Input — scope name + intent (or an existing spec for refine / pivot). Output —
    `specs/<scope>/<scope>.spec.md` (scope-type interface).

    Out of scope: implementation, module decomposition, product / library design. The project portal
    is the root branch.

    **Glossary.** Modes: greenfield · refine · pivot · rewrite. Consumers = the scopes that depend on this
    interface scope.
  </Mission>

  <BeliefState deps="AX_OPERATOR_LANGUAGE, AX_OPERATOR_DIALOGUE_STYLE, AX_DIALOGUE_DISCIPLINE, AX_OPERATOR_SAFEGUARD, AX_DIVERGE_BEFORE_RECOMMEND, AX_NO_PROCESS_NARRATION, AX_STATELESS_ARTIFACT, AX_SCALE_PROPORTIONAL_DEPTH">
    {{> "axiom/scaffold/ax-directive-mode"}}

    {{> "axiom/scaffold/ax-mode-auto-detect-or-halt"}}

    {{> "axiom/boundary/ax-portal-read-only-with-placeholder-exception"}}

    {{> "axiom/spec/ax-living-spec"}}

    {{> "axiom/spec/ax-spec-lifecycle"}}

    {{> "axiom/truth/ax-spec-is-sole-source"}}

    {{> "axiom/spec/ax-interface-flow"}}

    {{> "axiom/spec/ax-decision-log-required"}}

    {{> "axiom/spec/ax-pivot-requires-supersession"}}

    {{> "axiom/boundary/ax-cross-scope-dependencies"}}

    {{> "axiom/spec/ax-parallel-mechanism-requires-justification"}}

    {{> "axiom/truth/ax-evidence-hygiene"}}

    {{> "axiom/boundary/ax-bootstrap-narrow-read"}}

    <Axiom id="AX_SPEC_MANDATORY_DIAGRAM">
      Every interface spec carries at least one diagram in an `Overview` section, high up — who produces vs consumes the contract, or the version-transition flow, at a glance. The floor is one (mermaid or ASCII), held by tooling: `sdd-check` fails a missing section (`SDD_NO_DIAGRAM_BLOCK`) or an empty one (`SDD_DIAGRAM_BLOCK_EMPTY`). Beyond the floor the author adds more views by judgment; that is not a gate.
    </Axiom>

    {{> "axiom/process/ax-artifact-style-self-check"}}

    {{> "axiom/process/ax-close-with-integrity-check"}}
  </BeliefState>

  <HaltConditions>
    | 🛑 ID | Trigger |
    |---|---|
    | `H_NO_INTAKE` | Empty intake |
    | `H_AMBIGUOUS_MODE` | Spec exists + mode verb absent (per `AX_MODE_AUTO_DETECT_OR_HALT`) |
    | `H_BREAKING_CHANGE_NO_PROTOCOL` | A breaking interface change without a declared breaking-change protocol |
    | `H_SYSTEM_FIT_NOT_RUN` | `STEP_3_VERSIONING_POLICY` entered before `STEP_2B_SYSTEM_FIT`'s checklist closed, or "вводим новое" recorded without the specific neighbour invariant/requirement ID it fails (`AX_PARALLEL_MECHANISM_REQUIRES_JUSTIFICATION`) |
    | `H_PIVOT_NO_INVALIDATION_LIST` | `pivot` mode without a Pivot Invalidation List |
    | `H_REWRITE_WITH_DOWNSTREAM` | `rewrite` mode but the scope already has tickets — not v0, use `pivot` (`AX_PIVOT_REQUIRES_SUPERSESSION`) |
    | `H_BOOTSTRAP_REQUIREMENTS_MISSING` | External-deps step finished without a Bootstrap Requirements section |
    | `H_OPERATOR_REJECT` | Operator rejected the spec |
  </HaltConditions>

  <ExecutionPlan>
    <Step id="STEP_0_INTAKE">
      <Goal>Resolve scope name and mode.</Goal>
      <Action>
        State from the router gives the portal + scope-type (interface). Resolve the scope name; stat
        the spec → `greenfield` or detect the mode per `AX_DIRECTIVE_MODE` / `AX_MODE_AUTO_DETECT_OR_HALT`.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_1_CONFIRM">
      <Goal>Confirm interface and outline the section set.</Goal>
      <Action>Confirm scope-type, outline sections. Approval Check. STOP.</Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_2_INTERFACE_DECLARATION">
      <Goal>Declare the interface.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Per `AX_INTERFACE_FLOW`: schema format (OpenAPI / gRPC proto / JSON Schema / GraphQL),
        versioning scheme (semver / date-based / none), namespacing — Facts / Assumptions /
        Hypotheses separated per `AX_EVIDENCE_HYGIENE`. Then run the operator interview —
        `READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/interview-protocol.directive.xml")` — passing
        scope-type `interface` (selects the TopicCatalog block) and the confirmed `scale:` from
        the session file: per `AX_SCALE_PROPORTIONAL_DEPTH` `fix` / `function` → base topics + the
        triage minimum; `product` → the full scope-type block. The interview IS the substance of
        the step. Approval Check. STOP.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_2B_SYSTEM_FIT">
      <Goal>Reconcile with the existing system before the versioning policy locks.</Goal>
      <Action>
        FIRST action this step: run `npx gennady sdd-orient specs/<scope>/<scope>.spec.md --scope
        <scope>` (the path names where THIS interface spec lives even before `sdd-new` materializes
        it) and read its output in full: the portal line, the one-hop neighbours with their paths,
        entity/contract NAMES, requirement IDs + titles, the consumers list, and its closing question.

        Then close, in THIS message, the fixed checklist — record every answer in the spec (Decision
        Log entry when (a)/(b) lands on "new", inline note otherwise):
        (a) Is this contract / schema shape already an existing kind — does the extract already name
        it on a neighbour interface or a producer/consumer scope?
        (b) If not: which existing contract the extract names are we EXTENDING (a new version, a new
        field) instead of introducing a parallel one?
        (c) Which neighbour specs (paths, from the extract — producers, consumers) will need work for
        this to fit the system — each becomes its own «СОСЕДИ» line in the eventual `CHANGE_MANIFEST`
        / Pivot Invalidation List sideways entry?
        (d) Which neighbour requirements (IDs, from the extract) conflict with the versioning policy
        we are about to lock, and how is the conflict resolved?
        "Вводим новое" answers (a)/(b) ONLY together with the specific neighbour invariant/requirement
        ID the existing contract cannot satisfy, plus its own Decision Log entry
        (`AX_PARALLEL_MECHANISM_REQUIRES_JUSTIFICATION`) — else `H_SYSTEM_FIT_NOT_RUN`. On a
        genuinely greenfield project with no neighbours, `sdd-orient` degenerates to its one-line
        "соседей нет" — the checklist still runs, (a) still gets an honest answer, (c)/(d) collapse to
        "н/д"; the step itself is never skipped. STOP.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_3_VERSIONING_POLICY">
      <Goal>Lock the versioning policy.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Versioning scheme + breaking-change protocol + consumer-notification rule — each locked choice
        recorded as a Decision Log entry (`AX_DECISION_LOG_REQUIRED`, `DECISION_LOG_ENTRY_FORMAT`). A
        breaking change without a protocol → `H_BREAKING_CHANGE_NO_PROTOCOL`. STOP.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_4_COMPATIBILITY_MATRIX">
      <Goal>Lock compatibility guarantees and consumers.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Backward-compat guarantees + consumer declaration (which scopes consume this contract, per
        `AX_CROSS_SCOPE_DEPENDENCIES`). STOP.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_5_EXTERNAL_DEPENDENCIES_AUDIT">
      <Goal>Materialize Bootstrap Requirements.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Walk the drafted spec; extract external assumptions; classify `exists` | `missing` | `unknown`
        (narrow read for inventory only, per `AX_BOOTSTRAP_NARROW_READ` and `AX_SPEC_IS_SOLE_SOURCE` —
        design stays sourced from specs); resolve with the operator;
        materialize the Bootstrap Requirements table. Empty only if explicit «nothing to bootstrap»,
        else `H_BOOTSTRAP_REQUIREMENTS_MISSING`.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_6_FINAL_SPEC">
      <Goal>Emit the interface spec.</Goal>
      <Action>
        In `greenfield`/`rewrite` mode, when `specs/<scope>/<scope>.spec.md` does not exist yet,
        create its skeleton via `sdd-new interface --scope <scope>` — it never overwrites and prints
        the section manifest (which sections are REQUIRED and what to fill); in `refine`/`pivot` mode
        the file already exists, edit it in place, skip `sdd-new`. Content guidance per
        `READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/formats/interface-spec-structure.xml")`.
        Before writing, run the self-check pass per
        `AX_ARTIFACT_STYLE_SELF_CHECK`. In `refine` mode update sections in place per
        `AX_LIVING_SPEC`. In `pivot` mode also
        `READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/formats/pivot-formats.xml")`
        (`AX_PIVOT_REQUIRES_SUPERSESSION`); in `rewrite` mode write fresh — no supersession. For a brand-new scope, append the `🚧 (awaiting root sync)` placeholder row to the portal Scopes table per `AX_PORTAL_READ_ONLY_WITH_PLACEHOLDER_EXCEPTION` — every other portal edit belongs to the root flow. Write in review-state per `AX_SPEC_LIFECYCLE` — prepend a `CHANGE_MANIFEST` (`READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/formats/change-manifest.xml")`) and mark changed lines `✚`/`~` (greenfield → manifest only, no per-line marks) — its «СОСЕДИ» block carries the (c)/(d) answers `STEP_2B_SYSTEM_FIT` recorded, never left empty by omission; compress folds it to master downstream after the change ships. Then close with the integrity check per `AX_CLOSE_WITH_INTEGRITY_CHECK`: run `sdd-check --all specs/<scope>` (anchor balance + required sections + links) and resolve any finding. Then `READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/review-lifecycle.directive.xml")` — internal critic → publish (MR) → external review → compress + merge on approval. After the spec merges to master, handoff is to scaffold (interface scopes have no modules).
        Approval Check. STOP.
      </Action>
    </Step>
  </ExecutionPlan>

